          {
            "title": "Question 3",
            "id": 76924,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When might we need to check if two numbers are equal?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">When checking if a variable is exactly equal to 10</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">When checking if a variable is above 50</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">When checking if a variable is exactly equal to 10.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A cart stores <code>items = 10</code>. Which check matches exactly <code>10</code> items, not more or fewer?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Checking whether <code>items</code> is equal to <code>10</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Checking whether <code>items</code> is above <code>10</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Checking whether <code>items</code> is at least <code>10</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Checking whether <code>items</code> is equal to <code>10</code>.</p></body></html>"
