        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Inequality operator",
            "id": 76877,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To check if a number isn't equal to another number, we use the <strong>inequality operator</strong>, <code>!=</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" != \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"===\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>!=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To check if a number isn't equal to another number, we use the <strong>inequality operator</strong>, <code>!=</code>.</p><p>Add the operator so the comparison of <code>1</code> and <code>10</code> prints <code>True</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" != \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"!==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>!=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Inequality operator",
            "id": 76873,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can store the result of a comparison with the inequality operator in a variable like here where we'll store the comparison <code>1 != 2</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"result = \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" != \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(result)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"13\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>=</code>, followed by <code>!=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can store the result of a comparison in a variable.</p><p>Store whether <code>1</code> is not equal to <code>2</code> in <code>result</code> so the code prints <code>True</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"result = \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" != \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(result)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"13\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"!==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>=</code>, followed by <code>!=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Result ==",
            "id": 76875,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Variables can store the result of equality comparisons too, such as <code>result = 1 == 2</code>. </p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"result = \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(result)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"13\" /><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"6\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"False\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>result</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Variables can store the result of equality comparisons too.</p><p>Store whether <code>1</code> is equal to <code>2</code> in <code>result</code> so the code prints <code>False</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"result = \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(result)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"6\" /><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"13\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"!=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\":\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"False\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>result</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Compare variables",
            "id": 76871,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can compare values with variables and variables with other variables with <code>==</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"one = \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"two = \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(one == two)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(one != two)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"28\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"False\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 1",
            "id": 76868,
            "contentType": "interactive",
